You'll probably have to terminate him. Getting the charisma effect on a
magic trap has a high chance of taming success, but that's not
practical at all for your situation.

Since you can't retame him as he is, whack him with a rubber chicken,
lob a cockatrice egg in his direction, zap him with a wand of death, or
give him the Finger. You can then take all of his items, stuff them
into a container, then reanimate him via stone-to-flesh or undead
turning, then charm him again.

Or, if you don't mind not being able to respawn him, polymorph him into
a violet fungus and take all of the items off of him and give them to
the other Archon, or a new pet.

Of course, if Archons are still spawning, then just stone him and bash
him into pebbles, or give him the Finger and keep him as a souvenir
tin. Then again, if you have all of those wishes possible, why not just
wish for a blessed figurine of an Archon and not bother with the
original?



